  "tests_url": "https://github.com/davelab10/railcall-stripe-invoicing/blob/main/TESTING.md",
  "description": "Governed Stripe accounts receivable for RailCall Station. The module exposes 32 commands under stripe.billing.*: 19 read commands and 13 approval-controlled writes that stop at the Station airlock before any external mutation.\n\nBILLING AND COLLECTIONS\nbill_client is the composite monthly-billing path: normalized customer identity, safe optional billing_run_id metadata, strict financial validation, staged truthful outcomes, invoice item, finalization, and delivery behind one human approval. invoice_preview is local and effect-free. payment_status_summary and customer_balance_summary are read-only operational views.\n\nAI DECISION SUPPORT\npayment_risk_assess evaluates minimized aggregate payment metrics. collection_strategy_recommend returns a human-reviewable collections plan. billing_anomaly_detect reviews anonymized portfolio metrics. dunning_message_draft produces a privacy-minimized, structured draft without sending email or exposing customer/Stripe identifiers to the LLM. All four commands are read-only, structured, fail-closed decision support. AI never authorizes a charge or moves money.\n\nGOVERNANCE\nAll commands require receipts. The sandbox declares only Stripe and Groq network access, no subprocess capability, and no filesystem writes. Existing STRIPE_SECRET_KEY vault entries remain compatible with Station's Configure card and named credentials.\n\nRUNTIME EVIDENCE\nThe v1.4.0 migration remains project-owned and does not patch Station. Provider success is claimed only when supported by a real provider receipt; ambiguous write outcomes remain unknown and retain idempotency.\n\nDemo: https://youtu.be/7wtXK724Kig\n\ncontest:2026Q3",
  "license_required": false,
